+# Offline candidate scope
+
+Keep this adapter isolated from live bots and existing project state. Do not add network send, trading, model APIs, credentials, background services or source-text execution.
+Preserve the pinned upstream MIT files byte-for-byte; do not execute vendor scripts.
+Treat anchors and evidence sufficiency as analyst judgments. Aggregation is deterministic, missing weights are not normalized, and unresolved contradictions block their evidence requirements.
+Retain native abstention and hard-risk precedence. Keep monetary, price, currency and security-unit blocking scopes separate.
+Use synthetic or public fixtures only. Do not add private source content, names, paths, unrelated desktop screenshots or credentials. R1 explicitly permits actual screenshots of this public/synthetic dashboard as private review evidence.
+Run the focused standard-library and Node security tests described in README.md after relevant changes. Review the complete public diff before any future remote publication.
